_irNotes: {
	"decision-01": "The world is real 3D in Babylon.js on WebGPU: road, terrain, props and cars are meshes lit and painted by the gouache passes. Rejected: Out Run's pseudo-3D road projection, which holds no hills to stand props on, no camera moves and no painted models"
	"decision-02": "60Hz deterministic kinetic simulation conforms to Pronto algebraic isomorphism contracts with bit-exact rollback history"
	"decision-03": "Input is omnishell's createKineticInput, over its vendored game-inputs, with dual code/key matching and the Gamepad API"
	"decision-escape-hatches": "Escape hatches: the art pack seed (hatch-assets), and the renderer (renderer), a presenter whose worker paints the road and the HUD's fast readouts into the screen's canvas layers and does nothing else. The simulation is not a hatch: it is a Jessie engine (shell/engine/engine.js and the modules it imports) that the terminal's cage steps, endowed with nothing, and it lifts the run's milestones (grid, start, checkpoint, time over, finish) with the commands since the last. The sound is a Jessie role (shell/engine/sound.js) on the AudioContext the terminal tames. The race is the arena's Cortex kinetic child (pronto's kinetic-machine record): the terminal starts it on the screen's mount, and the run machine (shell/handlers/run.js, Jessie) folds what it lifts and what is pressed into the run row. No script of the app's own is served"
	"decision-leaderboard-writes": "The high-score table is public to read with its writes added in a raw migration, because the access model has no \"everyone reads, the owner inserts\" mode. The insert arm checks the row's player against the session; there is no update or delete arm and the privileges are revoked, so a score is a record and not a draft. A BEFORE INSERT trigger stamps the server's clock and admits one row per player per 75 s, the shortest any run can last; a redelivered insert carries the id it was minted with and passes the trigger untouched, so the gateway's ignore-duplicates absorbs it. Rejected: declaring the table private and widening its read in SQL, which would make it \"mine\" to the browser and \"everyone's\" to the server; and a per-run token from a server function, which an anonymous arcade does not need and which cannot make a modified client honest"
}

